<Defs>

  <!--
    The Sunken Vault (docs/design/peoples-third.md, the eighth of the eight; docs/design/peoples.md, "Release G";
    Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/PeoplesG2.cs): a sealed shelter whose people came up after generations below, with spacer
    gear and failing power cells. They cannot make what they carry, and every year a little more of it stops working.
    Spacer, on the game's outlander parent, and the one people that declines unless supplied (ageDeclines, 0.169.0's
    rule: an age about every four years with nothing, held by the components and parts the colony sells or gives them;
    never below the medieval age, ageFloor 1). They arise in the industrial and spacer ages (ariseAges 2~3: a shelter
    opened). The look: the vault suit in vault olive, a collar shirt and trousers of the one cloth with the vault's number
    on the back, worn and patched; in a later, poorer age patched with whatever is at hand (ageArms: a duster or a parka
    over it in the industrial age, a cape in the medieval age). Their security in recon armour with charge rifles at
    first, then flak and rifles, then plate and spears. A share are intellectuals and medics. Kinds of people: dirtmoles,
    stoneborn, insectors, korgs, genies, pigskins, wasters, vault-born every one. Gifts: a psylink for the overseer now
    and then (Protector), technomancers, super soldiers and rangers of A RimWorld of Magic, strong immunity in the medics.
    Their towns: the vault door in the hillside with a surface camp growing round it (Rimfolk_Plan_VaultDoor). At the
    gate: their last spacer goods for components and food (Rimfolk_Evt_VaultBarter); a craft they have lost, taught at the
    colony's bench (Rimfolk_Evt_VaultCraft); a vault-born child who has never seen a sky asks to stay
    (Rimfolk_Evt_VaultChild). Their ask: power cells, components for the vault's last machines
    (Rimfolk_Mission_VaultCells). Their founding: Overseer Hollis Crane broke the seal. Faith (Ideology): the vault below
    (tunneler), the overseer's word (loyalist) and Vanilla Ideology Expanded's scrapper.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="OutlanderFactionBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_SunkenVault</defName>
    <label>Sunken Vault</label>
    <description>The people of a sealed shelter that opened after generations below, who came up into a world that had not waited for them. They carry spacer gear their great-grandparents made and nobody alive can mend, and every year a little more of it stops working. They trade the last of it for components and food, ask other peoples to teach them the crafts they lost, and remember who kept them supplied.\n\nTheir ways began when the vault's water ran short, generations after the doors were sealed. The vault's council chose Overseer Hollis Crane to open them, and she broke the seal and walked out first into the light. Nobody had told them what the sky would be like, and half of them went back below for a week. The vault took its number from the door, and every dweller still wears it on the back of the suit.\n\nThey are careful, polite and a little afraid of open ground, and they count everything twice. They fear the last cell going dark, a door that will not close and the sky with nothing over it. A vault is kept by its warden, and the people by their overseer.</description>
    <pawnSingular>dweller</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>dwellers</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>overseer</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Spacer</techLevel>
    <basicMemberKind>Rimfolk_SunkenVault_Dweller</basicMemberKind>
    <factionNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_SunkenVault</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_SunkenVaultTown</settlementNameMaker>
    <factionIconPath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/SunkenVault</factionIconPath>
    <settlementTexturePath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/SunkenVaultTown</settlementTexturePath>
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.32, 0.34, 0.22)</li>
      <li>(0.52, 0.54, 0.36)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
    <hidden>false</hidden>
    <naturalEnemy>false</naturalEnemy>
    <permanentEnemy>false</permanentEnemy>
    <canSiege>false</canSiege>
